    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "but they’ll never see it that way. they see me as the one who made it, the one who was supposed to make it all worth it. seeing their faces just makes the guilt so much worse because i know they’re disappointed even if they don't say it. sometimes i think it would just be easier if i wasn't even part of the equation anymore. like, if i just wasn't here, the mistake wouldn't exist and they could just remember the version of me that actually succeeded.",
